<item>
<title>Telegram macOS</title>
<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats: set a phrase in Settings &gt; Privacy and Security &gt; Hidden Chats, then type it in chat search to open the chats you hide there. Everywhere else they stay out of sight, including the chat list, search, notifications, badges and calls&lt;br&gt;• Each phrase opens its own set of hidden chats. Leave with ⌘L or the Leave button; hidden chats also close on sleep, screen lock or after five idle minutes&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats are a Mac-only feature: phrases and hidden chats stay in this app on this Mac and don't sync, so your other devices keep showing these chats as usual&lt;br&gt;• Don't forget your phrase: it isn't stored anywhere and can't be recovered. Without it, those chats stay hidden on this Mac until you log out of Telegram here and log back in&lt;br&gt;• Dictator's remote control bot works in groups: /ask, /tldr and /draft answer only you, with buttons to send the answer to the chat or save it in the bot chat&lt;br&gt;• Ask Dictator inline in any chat with @yourbot followed by a question; answers that would reveal anything private go to the bot chat instead&lt;br&gt;• The bot paired with Dictator appears first when you type @ in a message&lt;br&gt;• Create polls in Saved Messages.&lt;br&gt;• Dictator: set it up with an AI agent such as Claude Code or Codex through the dictator command and its MCP server; the Home screen shows the commands to copy&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• The Global Search prompt for posts is centered and its button is a Liquid Glass capsule&lt;br&gt;• The chat moves smoothly when a bot's keyboard appears, changes or closes&lt;br&gt;• Updated to the latest Telegram core, including the new on-chain gift sales and offers&lt;br&gt;• Context menus use native Liquid Glass&lt;br&gt;• Profile gift previews now animate smoothly back into their bubbles when closed.&lt;br&gt;• The message composer and rich-text editor remember your last target language for translation.&lt;br&gt;• Group admins can moderate a participant’s reactions from the reactions menu, with VoiceOver support.&lt;br&gt;• Screen sharing in calls uses far less memory and CPU again&lt;br&gt;• Lower memory use in chats, profiles and the shared media grid, and after the app sits idle&lt;br&gt;• Chats that restrict saving content no longer use about 64 MB of extra graphics memory while open&lt;br&gt;• Protected media in the media viewer shows its real colors instead of oversaturated ones&lt;br&gt;• The emoji panel loads all packs when you open it instead of in every chat you visit&lt;br&gt;• Telegram gives back more memory while it sits unused, and interface strings take less memory and load faster&lt;br&gt;• Global post search shows placeholder rows as soon as you press Search and animates the query as you type&lt;br&gt;• Dictator: pairing and the settings that decide what the agent may do are now sealed in the Keychain; after this update Telegram asks once to connect Dictator again&lt;br&gt;• Dictator: the agent can open the app menus, the Dock and menu bar icons, and the text it types stays out of process arguments&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• Opening an unjoined channel could clear its messages behind a spinner a few seconds after they appeared&lt;br&gt;• The Optimizing Database screen and other early startup screens now appear in your language&lt;br&gt;• Paid messages send when your Stars balance exactly covers the price&lt;br&gt;• Bug fixes and improvements&lt;br&gt;• Crash fixes and stability improvements&lt;br&gt;• The Share window sends links, contacts, stories, QR codes, and comments to the selected forum topic.&lt;br&gt;• The media viewer stays on the same photo when new photos arrive.&lt;br&gt;• Public profile photos no longer show an incorrect date.&lt;br&gt;• Polls that allow new options keep Add Option available after you vote. Enabling anonymous voting turns off Add Option.&lt;br&gt;• Pressing Down in chat search no longer hangs when there are no recent chats. Return can open the top result after you change the search.&lt;br&gt;• Rich-message lists align their markers with the text and respect custom numbering. Nested media fits its column, and dividers are centered.&lt;br&gt;• Media slider previews in the rich-text editor keep spoilers covered. Plain-text copies put a quote and its author on separate lines.&lt;br&gt;</description>
